1
00:00:49,140 --> 00:00:52,990
[The Old Story of Yu Hong]

2
00:00:53,310 --> 00:00:55,800
[Episode 6]

3
00:00:58,240 --> 00:00:59,300
Juan, you're back.

4
00:01:01,350 --> 00:01:03,710
This is a colleague from
the Yingjin Municipal Bureau,

5
00:01:03,710 --> 00:01:04,310
He Liang.

6
00:01:05,200 --> 00:01:06,130
-Hello.
-Hello.

7
00:01:11,590 --> 00:01:14,120
Are you the one
investigating Zhao Changyou?

8
00:01:15,280 --> 00:01:17,260
I was the one who took your call.

9
00:01:18,210 --> 00:01:18,850
Yes.

10
00:01:19,480 --> 00:01:20,289
I came this time

11
00:01:20,289 --> 00:01:21,350
to ask for your help

12
00:01:21,500 --> 00:01:23,930
in investigating
Zhao Changyou's social connections,

13
00:01:23,930 --> 00:01:25,039
to see if we can find

14
00:01:25,039 --> 00:01:27,400
clues about other members
of the poaching gang.

15
00:01:27,400 --> 00:01:28,530
What a coincidence.

16
00:01:28,760 --> 00:01:30,220
I've already found a clue.

17
00:01:31,710 --> 00:01:32,430
Really?

18
00:01:32,430 --> 00:01:33,180
Really.

19
00:01:33,650 --> 00:01:34,539
Let me ask first.

20
00:01:34,539 --> 00:01:36,479
The money for investigating the clue

21
00:01:36,479 --> 00:01:38,080
was paid out of my own pocket.

22
00:01:38,140 --> 00:01:40,710
Can your Yingjin Municipal Bureau
reimburse it?

23
00:01:40,710 --> 00:01:41,430
Fifty.

24
00:01:51,900 --> 00:01:52,729
Thirty-five.

25
00:02:00,090 --> 00:02:00,840
Fifteen.

26
00:02:06,840 --> 00:02:08,570
Just reimburse me a little bit.

27
00:02:08,910 --> 00:02:09,800
I can't.

28
00:02:10,860 --> 00:02:13,650
I searched everywhere
within a five-kilometer radius.

29
00:02:13,650 --> 00:02:14,470
Only this man

30
00:02:14,470 --> 00:02:16,870
has seen the guy
who ate with Zhao Changyou.

31
00:02:18,800 --> 00:02:20,150
We should start with the people

32
00:02:20,150 --> 00:02:21,410
around Zhao Changyou.

33
00:02:21,460 --> 00:02:22,720
Start with his family.

34
00:02:22,840 --> 00:02:23,400
Okay.

35
00:02:23,910 --> 00:02:25,410
The chief told me to assist you.

36
00:02:25,410 --> 00:02:26,940
We'll do it however you say.

37
00:02:28,780 --> 00:02:30,980
Can't you really reimburse me a little?

38
00:02:31,190 --> 00:02:34,450
No receipt, no invoice—
how am I supposed to reimburse you?

39
00:02:37,970 --> 00:02:40,970
Look at what she drew for me.
It's like being poisoned.

40
00:02:41,250 --> 00:02:42,430
It's wild, the way she drew it.

41
00:02:42,430 --> 00:02:44,020
It's actually p-pretty good.

42
00:02:44,020 --> 00:02:46,370
No, it's beautiful.

43
00:02:46,810 --> 00:02:49,000
"Ho leung"? What's that?

44
00:02:49,690 --> 00:02:50,820
What are you saying?

45
00:02:51,250 --> 00:02:53,780
She said it's beautiful.

46
00:02:57,130 --> 00:02:58,860
You can understand Cantonese?

47
00:02:59,190 --> 00:03:00,150
Of course.

48
00:03:00,520 --> 00:03:02,710
I loved watching Hong Kong movies
when I was a kid.

49
00:03:02,710 --> 00:03:05,180
And I love Hong Kong songs.

50
00:03:06,530 --> 00:03:07,150
Singer.

51
00:03:11,310 --> 00:03:13,870
Have you ever heard a song called

52
00:03:14,130 --> 00:03:15,690
"What Do I Seek in Life"?

53
00:03:18,030 --> 00:03:19,230
Let me sing it for you.

54
00:03:20,520 --> 00:03:22,500
♪ Cold and warm, when can they rest? ♪

55
00:03:24,090 --> 00:03:26,280
♪ Looking back, how many autumns? ♪

56
00:03:27,860 --> 00:03:30,420
♪ Searched everywhere, yet lost instead ♪

57
00:03:29,000 --> 00:03:30,400
Putting on a concert now.

58
00:03:30,800 --> 00:03:32,800
♪ What I didn't hope for is in my hand. ♪

59
00:03:34,000 --> 00:03:35,650
♪ Did I get it or not? ♪

60
00:03:36,000 --> 00:03:39,090
♪ Can't explain the gains and losses,
the mistakes ♪

61
00:03:39,090 --> 00:03:42,400
♪ Just heard and saw, then it changed ♪

62
00:03:42,400 --> 00:03:44,300
♪ Da da la li da la ♪

63
00:03:44,900 --> 00:03:46,100
I don't know the rest.

64
00:03:47,250 --> 00:03:48,090
Done singing.

65
00:03:48,740 --> 00:03:50,240
What's your name?

66
00:03:50,240 --> 00:03:52,120
My name is Qianqian.

67
00:03:52,870 --> 00:03:54,120
Qianqian.

68
00:03:54,120 --> 00:03:56,780
Is it the "Qianqian"
from "Thousands of Songs"?

69
00:03:57,410 --> 00:03:59,000
It's Qianqian.

70
00:03:59,000 --> 00:04:00,500
Qianqian.

71
00:04:01,860 --> 00:04:03,370
You two do the work.

72
00:04:03,370 --> 00:04:04,810
I can't even get a word in.

73
00:04:04,810 --> 00:04:06,460
-You're a bit extra.
-Draw it well.

74
00:04:06,460 --> 00:04:07,340
So extra.

75
00:04:09,870 --> 00:04:10,810
It's getting late.

76
00:04:10,810 --> 00:04:12,270
I'll go find a guesthouse.

77
00:04:12,500 --> 00:04:14,100
Well, we'll start tomorrow.

78
00:04:15,120 --> 00:04:16,720
Why don't you stay at a hotel?

79
00:04:16,860 --> 00:04:19,500
How much do they reimburse you
per day for travel?

80
00:04:19,500 --> 00:04:21,800
No reimbursement. Fifty yuan a day

81
00:04:21,800 --> 00:04:22,770
for allowance.

82
00:04:24,390 --> 00:04:25,270
So you mean,

83
00:04:25,270 --> 00:04:26,180
if you don't spend

84
00:04:26,180 --> 00:04:27,600
all this money in a day,

85
00:04:28,160 --> 00:04:29,540
then the rest is yours?

86
00:04:32,870 --> 00:04:34,180
Don't find me anything too expensive.

87
00:04:34,180 --> 00:04:35,310
I can stay anywhere.

88
00:04:36,870 --> 00:04:37,870
Well, you know...

89
00:04:38,740 --> 00:04:39,720
Guesthouses are too expensive.

90
00:04:39,720 --> 00:04:40,770
I know a place.

91
00:04:41,000 --> 00:04:42,800
Cheap and convenient.

92
00:04:43,510 --> 00:04:44,640
And meals included.

93
00:04:46,750 --> 00:04:47,890
There's a place like that?

94
00:04:47,890 --> 00:04:49,550
How come I don't know about it?

95
00:04:56,040 --> 00:04:56,970
Come in, please.

96
00:04:57,250 --> 00:04:58,909
No need to take off your shoes.

97
00:05:02,010 --> 00:05:03,120
Pretty nice, huh?

98
00:05:03,120 --> 00:05:04,450
It's so warm in here.

99
00:05:08,130 --> 00:05:09,370
This is your place?

100
00:05:10,570 --> 00:05:11,430
This...

101
00:05:11,860 --> 00:05:13,310
isn't appropriate, is it?

102
00:05:13,310 --> 00:05:15,110
What's inappropriate about it?

103
00:05:15,250 --> 00:05:16,050
You'll stay in this room.

104
00:05:16,050 --> 00:05:17,380
I'll clean it up for you.

105
00:05:17,480 --> 00:05:20,010
A guesthouse costs thirty a day—
so expensive.

106
00:05:20,010 --> 00:05:21,190
And breakfast isn't included.

107
00:05:21,190 --> 00:05:23,070
Staying here costs you only twenty yuan.

108
00:05:23,070 --> 00:05:24,770
You eat whatever we eat for dinner.

109
00:05:24,770 --> 00:05:27,920
And for breakfast,
there are steamed buns, eggs,

110
00:05:27,920 --> 00:05:29,250
and fried dough sticks.

111
00:05:30,040 --> 00:05:30,750
It's up to you.

112
00:05:30,750 --> 00:05:32,409
You can eat whatever you want.

113
00:05:32,510 --> 00:05:35,640
It's not really proper,
a man and a woman alone together.

114
00:05:36,510 --> 00:05:38,130
You're afraid I've got ideas about you?

115
00:05:38,130 --> 00:05:39,070
No way.

116
00:05:40,040 --> 00:05:41,370
I've practiced boxing.

117
00:05:41,690 --> 00:05:43,270
Y-You're overthinking it.

118
00:05:43,270 --> 00:05:44,870
You're not my type.

119
00:05:46,010 --> 00:05:47,540
Let me be straight with you.

120
00:05:48,240 --> 00:05:49,560
I just want to…

121
00:05:50,510 --> 00:05:51,640
make a little money.

122
00:05:54,860 --> 00:05:56,990
I like sticky bean buns in the morning.

123
00:05:57,420 --> 00:05:58,220
Alright.

124
00:05:58,570 --> 00:05:59,970
I'll get it ready for you.

125
00:06:03,070 --> 00:06:04,980
Twenty a day.

126
00:06:05,870 --> 00:06:07,920
Minus food, I can save fifteen.

127
00:06:07,920 --> 00:06:09,900
Four days, that's sixty.

128
00:06:10,570 --> 00:06:11,480
Forty-eight yuan.

129
00:06:11,480 --> 00:06:12,810
That already covers it.

130
00:06:15,950 --> 00:06:17,350
I can still make a little.

131
00:06:18,570 --> 00:06:20,900
Alright. A little is better than nothing.

132
00:06:21,190 --> 00:06:22,950
I'll teach you a sentence in Mandarin,

133
00:06:22,950 --> 00:06:24,810
and you teach me one in Cantonese.

134
00:06:24,950 --> 00:06:25,810
How about that?

135
00:06:25,830 --> 00:06:26,980
Good morning.

136
00:06:27,450 --> 00:06:28,630
Good morning.

137
00:06:28,860 --> 00:06:30,000
Sleep.

138
00:06:30,000 --> 00:06:31,750
-Sleep.
-I asked you to teach her Mandarin.

139
00:06:31,750 --> 00:06:33,540
Why are you learning Cantonese from her?

140
00:06:33,540 --> 00:06:34,830
We're learning from each other here.

141
00:06:34,830 --> 00:06:35,930
That won't do.

142
00:06:35,930 --> 00:06:37,450
If you teach her, I'll feed you.

143
00:06:37,450 --> 00:06:37,980
If she teaches you,

144
00:06:37,980 --> 00:06:39,780
you have to pay me five more yuan.

145
00:06:40,950 --> 00:06:42,800
Why are you such a money-grubber?

146
00:06:42,800 --> 00:06:44,800
I used to be carefree,
just feeding myself.

147
00:06:44,800 --> 00:06:45,390
Then my ex-husband

148
00:06:45,390 --> 00:06:46,740
suddenly dumped the kid on me,

149
00:06:46,740 --> 00:06:47,720
and doesn't give child support.

150
00:06:47,720 --> 00:06:48,800
What am I supposed to do?

151
00:06:48,800 --> 00:06:50,070
I have to find a way to make some money

152
00:06:50,070 --> 00:06:50,840
to raise her.

153
00:06:55,120 --> 00:06:57,060
When is her dad going to pick her up?

154
00:06:57,060 --> 00:06:58,330
He tricked me before.

155
00:06:58,330 --> 00:06:59,560
I've called him several times.

156
00:06:59,560 --> 00:07:01,070
He said he'd pick her up in two weeks.

157
00:07:01,070 --> 00:07:02,070
Now another week's gone by.

158
00:07:02,070 --> 00:07:04,390
I called again. No one answered,
and his phone is out of service.

159
00:07:04,390 --> 00:07:06,220
Her parents don't want her anymore.

160
00:07:06,220 --> 00:07:07,350
She's stuck with me.

161
00:07:09,130 --> 00:07:11,390
Why don't I just
send her to an orphanage?

162
00:07:11,920 --> 00:07:13,320
Send her to an orphanage?

163
00:07:16,740 --> 00:07:17,540
How did she...

164
00:07:18,250 --> 00:07:19,690
understand that?

165
00:07:19,690 --> 00:07:21,000
I'm just kidding.

166
00:07:21,500 --> 00:07:22,320
Just kidding.

167
00:07:22,980 --> 00:07:24,360
Don't go. Just stay here.

168
00:07:24,360 --> 00:07:24,740
Okay?

169
00:07:24,740 --> 00:07:25,560
Look at

170
00:07:25,770 --> 00:07:26,950
her long face.

171
00:07:30,680 --> 00:07:31,360
Let's go, Qianqian.

172
00:07:31,360 --> 00:07:32,760
-Let's go.
-Heading out.

173
00:07:34,010 --> 00:07:34,890
Is she heavy?

174
00:07:35,270 --> 00:07:35,870
It's okay.

175
00:07:38,810 --> 00:07:41,130
Kids learn languages
way faster than adults.

176
00:07:41,130 --> 00:07:43,390
You should watch
what you say around her.

177
00:07:43,800 --> 00:07:44,480
Got it.

178
00:07:44,930 --> 00:07:46,370
How's this kid

179
00:07:46,370 --> 00:07:47,680
so sharp?

180
00:07:48,250 --> 00:07:49,310
She sure doesn't take after her dad.

181
00:07:49,310 --> 00:07:51,680
Her dad couldn't even
pass Chinese back in the day.

182
00:07:51,680 --> 00:07:52,620
There was a question once

183
00:07:52,620 --> 00:07:54,770
asking who the author of "Midnight" was.

184
00:07:54,770 --> 00:07:55,830
Her dad saw the character "zi",

185
00:07:55,830 --> 00:07:57,740
thought it meant a chess piece,

186
00:07:58,430 --> 00:08:00,000
and guessed Nie Weiping.

187
00:08:01,420 --> 00:08:03,350
So what did you see in him back then?

188
00:08:03,510 --> 00:08:04,570
He looked mature.

189
00:08:05,120 --> 00:08:06,320
He was a sweet talker.

190
00:08:09,500 --> 00:08:10,830
Sweet-talking is easy.

191
00:08:12,930 --> 00:08:14,260
Come here. Hold my hand.

192
00:08:15,690 --> 00:08:16,310
Let's go.

193
00:08:18,240 --> 00:08:19,070
The wind is

194
00:08:20,130 --> 00:08:20,860
howling.

195
00:08:21,130 --> 00:08:24,460
A kidney transplant costs
at least 200,000 to 300,000 yuan.

196
00:08:25,060 --> 00:08:26,420
The hospitals here

197
00:08:26,420 --> 00:08:28,080
can't do that kind of surgery.

198
00:08:28,890 --> 00:08:30,420
We'd have to go to Shanghai.

199
00:08:31,300 --> 00:08:32,720
The money I've earned these past two years

200
00:08:32,720 --> 00:08:34,780
has all gone to my sister's dialysis.

201
00:08:34,960 --> 00:08:36,270
400 yuan a session.

202
00:08:37,789 --> 00:08:39,370
Just hearing that is scary.

203
00:08:40,460 --> 00:08:41,289
Now the three of us

204
00:08:41,289 --> 00:08:43,090
are living off my mom's pension.

205
00:08:45,360 --> 00:08:47,620
My mom's mind isn't working well either—

206
00:08:48,580 --> 00:08:49,910
one minute she's clear,

207
00:08:50,620 --> 00:08:51,950
the next she's out of it.

208
00:08:53,500 --> 00:08:55,300
My sister took over my mom's job.

209
00:08:56,550 --> 00:08:58,810
And it's a contract job at the bookstore.

210
00:08:59,270 --> 00:09:00,340
Pays crap.

211
00:09:00,770 --> 00:09:02,100
Even if we save it all up,

212
00:09:02,790 --> 00:09:04,050
we're still far short.

213
00:09:07,080 --> 00:09:08,410
What am I supposed to do?

214
00:09:14,340 --> 00:09:15,010
San Yan'er.

215
00:09:17,630 --> 00:09:18,890
Get me a job.

216
00:09:20,470 --> 00:09:28,790
[Golden Imperial Dance Hall]

217
00:09:23,530 --> 00:09:24,660
Whose place is this?

218
00:09:25,010 --> 00:09:25,870
Take a guess.

219
00:09:26,120 --> 00:09:27,200
It's also Dong's?

220
00:09:28,030 --> 00:09:28,750
Let's go.

221
00:09:29,080 --> 00:09:29,820
Hello.

222
00:09:30,940 --> 00:09:32,270
It's like our own place.

223
00:09:34,080 --> 00:09:35,880
Does Dong sell cigarettes here?

224
00:09:36,050 --> 00:09:37,960
Selling cigarettes is just a small part.

225
00:09:37,960 --> 00:09:39,910
The dance hall and all that
are all Dong's.

226
00:09:39,910 --> 00:09:41,320
Dong's got a big business.

227
00:09:41,320 --> 00:09:43,750
He usually talks business
with people here.

228
00:09:43,750 --> 00:09:45,250
Hello, Yun.

229
00:09:45,870 --> 00:09:48,390
Hi, baby. Brother Yan'er is here.

230
00:09:52,860 --> 00:09:54,010
Business.

231
00:09:54,500 --> 00:09:55,870
It's all business.

232
00:09:55,870 --> 00:09:57,080
Dong and I are good friends.

233
00:09:57,080 --> 00:09:57,670
When we meet up,

234
00:09:57,670 --> 00:09:58,670
he'll arrange a job for you.

235
00:09:58,670 --> 00:09:59,670
No problem at all.

236
00:10:13,860 --> 00:10:15,320
You look so cool, Dong.

237
00:10:15,650 --> 00:10:16,650
That flying move.

238
00:10:18,820 --> 00:10:19,410
Cool, huh?

239
00:10:19,410 --> 00:10:21,630
-So cool. Badass.
-Cool.

240
00:10:22,410 --> 00:10:24,140
Why are you grinning like that?

241
00:10:24,510 --> 00:10:26,550
This is my buddy.
The ride-or-die kind.

242
00:10:26,550 --> 00:10:27,960
We've been friends
since we were in diapers.

243
00:10:27,960 --> 00:10:29,220
He's looking for a job.

244
00:10:31,440 --> 00:10:33,370
What do you mean, looking for a job?

245
00:10:33,720 --> 00:10:35,000
What can he do?

246
00:10:35,940 --> 00:10:38,170
He graduated from
a railway technical school.

247
00:10:38,170 --> 00:10:39,050
He's educated.

248
00:10:39,050 --> 00:10:40,250
And loyal as hell.

249
00:10:40,550 --> 00:10:42,590
When we were kids,
I fell into a manure pit.

250
00:10:42,590 --> 00:10:44,120
Nobody would help me.

251
00:10:44,120 --> 00:10:46,080
He just grabbed me and yanked me out.

252
00:10:46,080 --> 00:10:47,360
I really admire him.

253
00:10:49,340 --> 00:10:51,140
The young man looks quite sharp.

254
00:10:52,100 --> 00:10:54,080
But pulling people out of a manure pit

255
00:10:54,080 --> 00:10:55,320
isn't much of a skill.

256
00:10:55,870 --> 00:10:57,410
I... I can do anything.

257
00:10:57,700 --> 00:10:59,830
Whatever makes money fast, I'll do it.

258
00:11:00,740 --> 00:11:02,200
Killing makes money fast.

259
00:11:02,500 --> 00:11:03,430
You got the guts?

260
00:11:18,360 --> 00:11:19,760
Including the burrying?

261
00:11:31,860 --> 00:11:32,600
Yang,

262
00:11:33,240 --> 00:11:34,550
what are you saying?

263
00:11:34,550 --> 00:11:35,910
Dong is just joking.

264
00:11:35,910 --> 00:11:36,890
This is all legit business.

265
00:11:36,890 --> 00:11:39,340
Killing? What a scary thing to say.

266
00:11:46,080 --> 00:11:47,080
Did you hear that?

267
00:11:49,240 --> 00:11:50,390
You little brat.

268
00:11:51,030 --> 00:11:53,090
Got some nerve joking like that, huh?

269
00:11:53,170 --> 00:11:54,050
Dong,

270
00:11:54,050 --> 00:11:54,820
he just—

271
00:11:58,980 --> 00:12:00,710
You think I do everything here?

272
00:12:01,170 --> 00:12:02,580
I run a legit nightclub.

273
00:12:07,670 --> 00:12:09,360
Then, Dong, how about...

274
00:12:10,580 --> 00:12:11,870
you do me a favor

275
00:12:11,870 --> 00:12:13,270
and arrange a job for him?

276
00:12:14,500 --> 00:12:16,370
Who do you think you are?

277
00:12:17,770 --> 00:12:18,620
Well, bro.

278
00:12:19,150 --> 00:12:20,170
You've seen it yourself.

279
00:12:20,170 --> 00:12:22,100
I pull in plenty of money every day.

280
00:12:22,270 --> 00:12:23,410
But with all the mouths to feed,

281
00:12:23,410 --> 00:12:25,010
I've got to support them all.

282
00:12:25,670 --> 00:12:27,400
Every position is filled here.

283
00:12:27,440 --> 00:12:29,770
He hasn't even figured out
his own job yet.

284
00:12:30,700 --> 00:12:31,650
Later,

285
00:12:32,010 --> 00:12:33,810
if we need a waiter or something,

286
00:12:35,360 --> 00:12:36,820
I'll have him let you know.

287
00:12:38,320 --> 00:12:39,120
Okay?

288
00:12:40,940 --> 00:12:41,870
Thank you, Dong.

289
00:12:51,440 --> 00:12:52,250
I'm going to restock later.

290
00:12:52,250 --> 00:12:53,840
Why don't you come with me?

291
00:12:54,130 --> 00:12:55,790
I'll split the money with you.

292
00:12:56,150 --> 00:12:56,750
Then aren't we

293
00:12:56,750 --> 00:12:58,360
doing the same job?

294
00:12:58,890 --> 00:13:00,620
I might as well just lie at home.

295
00:13:03,700 --> 00:13:04,670
Fair point.

296
00:13:10,050 --> 00:13:11,030
You go first.

297
00:13:12,000 --> 00:13:12,750
My stomach feels weird.

298
00:13:12,750 --> 00:13:14,210
I'm going up to take a dump.

299
00:13:15,370 --> 00:13:16,370
I'm leaving then.

300
00:13:17,700 --> 00:13:19,080
Take a dump for me too.

301
00:13:22,820 --> 00:13:23,630
Yeah.

302
00:14:04,460 --> 00:14:05,250
Dong.

303
00:14:08,050 --> 00:14:09,790
I came back to talk to you again.

304
00:14:10,410 --> 00:14:12,080
The main thing is,

305
00:14:13,600 --> 00:14:15,860
my family member is sick,

306
00:14:15,860 --> 00:14:17,960
so I'm a bit tight on money.

307
00:14:19,240 --> 00:14:21,030
How about you give me a chance?

308
00:14:21,550 --> 00:14:22,580
I'll do anything.

309
00:14:48,500 --> 00:14:49,170
Come on.

310
00:14:50,000 --> 00:14:51,260
Come in and let's talk.

311
00:14:54,860 --> 00:14:55,530
Go ahead.

312
00:14:56,030 --> 00:14:57,290
What kind of business?

313
00:14:57,460 --> 00:14:59,520
I want to hire you to take someone out.

314
00:15:00,980 --> 00:15:02,700
50,000 yuan to kill someone?

315
00:15:03,200 --> 00:15:05,330
I'll pay the other half when it's done.

316
00:15:05,820 --> 00:15:06,950
Who do you want dead?

317
00:15:07,500 --> 00:15:09,200
The boss of Wenwu Lubricants,

318
00:15:09,550 --> 00:15:10,480
Li Dewu.

319
00:15:10,910 --> 00:15:11,960
Li Dewu?

320
00:15:14,120 --> 00:15:17,320
The one who always
goes to Shasha Hair Salon, right?

321
00:15:17,910 --> 00:15:18,440
Okay.

322
00:15:19,100 --> 00:15:20,500
Go back and wait for news.

323
00:15:20,840 --> 00:15:22,640
I'll let you know when it's done.

324
00:15:35,120 --> 00:15:36,620
When did you come in?

325
00:15:37,440 --> 00:15:38,480
Did you come back to steal my money?

326
00:15:38,480 --> 00:15:39,130
No.

327
00:15:40,130 --> 00:15:41,580
I came back to talk to you.

328
00:15:42,340 --> 00:15:43,250
What do you want to talk about?

329
00:15:43,250 --> 00:15:44,320
You scared me.

330
00:15:44,320 --> 00:15:45,670
San Yan'er's good-for-nothing.

331
00:15:45,670 --> 00:15:47,930
I was afraid you'd think I'm useless too.

332
00:15:51,790 --> 00:15:52,890
I'll take the job.

333
00:15:55,000 --> 00:15:56,250
Wait, you heard all that?

334
00:15:56,250 --> 00:15:57,840
I was just fooling him.

335
00:15:57,840 --> 00:15:58,480
Dude.

336
00:15:58,840 --> 00:16:00,290
I run a legit nightclub.

337
00:16:00,290 --> 00:16:01,370
I'm not a gangster.

338
00:16:01,370 --> 00:16:02,830
Didn't you take his money?

339
00:16:02,960 --> 00:16:04,050
50,000 yuan out there

340
00:16:04,050 --> 00:16:05,620
is only enough to take off an arm.

341
00:16:05,620 --> 00:16:06,550
I can still do it.

342
00:16:08,010 --> 00:16:10,610
Wait, are you really
that desperate for money?

343
00:16:15,580 --> 00:16:16,480
Can you do it for 20,000 yuan?

344
00:16:16,480 --> 00:16:17,120
Yes.

345
00:16:19,720 --> 00:16:20,270
Thanks.
